Z||000005||Slammed Fiero||05-30-2001||05:05 PM||||93's were not L98's , you couldn't get a Tpi caprice. The L98 has more stump pulling torque than the Lt1 , but runs out of breath at around 4800rpm , L98 redlines at 5600rpm with a factory spark interup, as a pose to the fiero's fuel cut off. The best L98 to get is the Vette motor from mid 86 on , make sure it's mid 86 or you may wind up getting an iron head motor , or a 86 convert , all which were equiped with aluminum heads. Rated at 240hp. 87 changed to a different cam rated at 245hp and good for 14.0's in a vette (I have an 87 with 18,00 miles on it)<P>94 is the first year for the LT1 in a caprice. Rated at 260hp it uses cast iron heads and a crank driven clutched fan.<P>The Impala SS motor is identical but uses an electric fan.<P>The Camaro motor is basically the same with the main exception being the aluminum heads.<P>all above are 2 bolt main motors.<P>The Caprice's ECM Limits top speed to 108MPH , The impala SS has no limiter. If you get a caprice motor , you may be able to change it with the Impala SS or Camaro ECM. The Chips are hard wired , in order to reprogram the ECM's you need a power programmer. It would probably be cheaper to find an ECM from a Camaro or Impala.<P>Keep in mind the Lt1 was also put in a few caprice wagons , and all roadmaster / roadmaster wagons from 94 to 96. Some rare Caddies had RWD Lt1's but not sure what models , and I know they were short production run cars.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Pontiaddict||05-30-2001||06:53 PM||||The Caddies were Fleetwoods.<BR>The other Caprice motors were the TBI powered 5.7 and 4.3L v8's.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Black88GT||05-30-2001||07:23 PM||||Slammed, do you know if you can put the Corvette alum. heads on the Impala SS motor?  Or would it be like putting alum. heads on a Fiero motor (i.e. pain in the butt)?||||reg||1
Z||000008||Slammed Fiero||05-30-2001||09:09 PM||||Our 94 Impala SS-ized Caprice wagoon has/ had an iron head LT1 , it now has Aluminum heads from an LT4 , it's a farily common conversion. It used to be offered as a GM perf upgrade , don't know if this was just through dealers , or factory backed. We got our kit from Scogin Dickey Chev olds.<P>So the answer is yes it will bolt up rather easily<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
